      "description": "<p>This live blog is now closed.</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/feb/17/sign-up-for-the-breaking-news-us-email-to-get-newsletter-alerts-direct-to-your-inbox?utm_medium=ACQUISITIONS_STANDFIRST&amp;utm_campaign=BN22326&amp;utm_content=signup&amp;utm_term=standfirst&amp;utm_source=GUARDIAN_WEB\">Sign up for the Breaking News US email</a></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/community/live/2026/oct/05/reader-q-a-iran-war-trump-midterms-reporter-answers\">Ask our reporters your questions about the Iran war and the US midterms</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>As the supreme court hears oral arguments this morning, it’s worth noting that if the justices side with Boulder or decide that the case is not in their jurisdiction, then it would continue in state court.</strong></p><p>But if the fossil fuel industry convinces the justices, the decision could apply not only to the Boulder case, but also to the many other climate cases brought by state and local governments around the US that we mentioned earlier.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/oct/05/donald-trump-nebraska-midterms-republicans-white-house-media-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
